# S-PROBE — Extraction Feasibility Spike: System Design

## 0. Scope of this document

This is the **DESIGN** artifact for the S-PROBE spike. It specifies the component graph,
interfaces, data flow, and state machines for a probe whose *product* is the file
`reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`.

It does **not** contain the probe's results. The probe was not executed — see §8 (Blockers).
The design is deliberately **parametric over the SAEOS-1 §4.3 node-type schema** and over the
sealed-goal corpus, so that execution is a mechanical pass once those two inputs exist.

---

## 1. What the probe is trying to falsify

SAEOS-1 §9/A8 is (per the goal statement) the assumption that **sealed goals contain enough
structured residue to be mechanically extracted into the §4.3 node types**. A spike that cannot
fail is not a spike. The design therefore fixes the falsification condition *before* any goal is
read:

> **H0 (the claim under test):** for a representative sealed goal, the §4.3 node types can be
> populated from the goal's existing artifacts with acceptable information loss.
>
> **Falsified when:** `loss_ratio > loss_threshold` (§5.3), or when any node type is
> **structurally unpopulable** (every one of its required fields `absent` across all 3 goals) —
> the latter is a NO-GO regardless of the aggregate ratio (§5.4, R-2).

Pre-registering the threshold and the tie-breaks is the whole point: it removes the degree of
freedom that would let a motivated executor land on GO.

